    whereEn: 'Chore divisions, punctuality disputes, financial disagreements, and in-law relations.',
    misconceptionsEn: 'Myth: "Generous attribution means tolerating chronic abuse." Fact: Generous attribution applies to normal human errors in healthy partners; chronic patterns of deliberate harm require firm boundaries.',
    limitationsEn: 'If a partner is actively deceitful or abusive, attributing their behavior to external stress enables toxicity; situational grace requires mutual goodwill.',
